l provide the podcast free  of charge and then they will charge for  a worksheet for a lesson for  explanations or possibly for the  transcript  our model is different we have some  beginner podcasts  and we mix in with those  what i would call authentic  everyday native speakers speaking to  each other type of podcasts  what i want to explore at link is the  extent to which  a language learner can start learning  the language with real language rather  than beginner language we offer the  beginner language i think most learners  seem to prefer the beginner language but  i think that it is quite possible to use  uh small doses of authentic language and  link  and listen over and over again to this  content and really improve in the  language quite quickly  so we are looking for people to help us  because while i have uh done some  podcasts in japanese and french and  spanish and german and swedish  it's for even chinese it's preferable  that these podcasts be  uh conversations occasionally the odd  monologue but it should involve native  speakers so we have put the word out and  i by this very podcast and and youtube i  want to put the word out  people out there  why not join our community that link  uh  give us a podcast  five minutes ten minutes  10 minutes preferable i think that's a  good length  talk to your husband wife friend  mother  child  talk about what you do whether you live  in  in buenos aires or  you know  athens or singapore  it doesn't matter people are interested  in hearing about other people in the  world  now this has started we've received some  very interesting spanish language  podcasts from people night clubbing in  buenos aires or a  mexican and chilean couple talking about  the different foods that they like to  cook  and  we would like people  to help us with podcasts and we are  prepared  to give points because some of you may  know that at link a lot of the functions  are free however in order to access our  tutors or to have writing corrected you  need points but we are willing to pay  points we're willing to pay a thousand  points for a ten minute podcast  so  right now we're going to limit it to the  languages that are available at link  which is of course english french  spanish german  russian  portuguese italian  chinese japanese i don't think i left  anything out  if you are a native speaker of any of  those languages  if you have  an interest  people seem to either use audacity  a-u-d-a-c-i-t-y  as a recording software or with the mac  wiretap studios is a very good piece of  software audacity happens to be free  and they produce these mp3 files  i think generally speaking a usb  microphone gives better sound quality  uh  often the sound quality will also depend  on the sound card in your in your  computer we're quite happy to provide  technical advice for people  but we would really like to collect it's  almost like a wiki  uh we would like to collect the voices  of people  uh wherever they are  talking about their lives or local  events or things of interest or what  makes their particular region  attractive or or what are special  features or customs or  uh  seasons of the year or whatever it might  be ten minutes long conversations are  preferred and we don't mind if you s  whatever regional variant or accent you  have in your language  we're very interested in in receiving  podcasts as i say we will compensate  people with points  for the podcast that we use  you don't have to worry about  transcribing them because we will  transcribe them  so we look forward to hearing from  people who would like to  join our  link series of  podcasts uh please let me know if you're  interested you can contact us  at  customer service at link lingq.com  uh i look forward to hearing from you  thank you

